e and testimony from the Nuremberg trials, British Foreign Office reports, and the author's recollection of his six years in Germany (from 1934 to 1940) as a journalist, reporting on Nazi Germany for newspapers, the United Press International (UPI), and CBS Radio.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rise_and_Fall_of_the_Third_Reich","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"The Rise and Fall of the Third Reich: A History of Nazi Germany","author":"William L. Shirer","publisher":"Simon & Schuster","publicationDate":"October 17, 1960","publicationPlace":"United States","pages":"1,249","language":"English"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-the-rise-and-fall-of-the-third-reich-william-l-shirer"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-hillman-book-journalism-hillman-prize-previous-honorees-1961","label":"Hillman Prize previous honorees: 1961","url":"https://www.hillmanfoundation.org/hillman-prizes/us/honorees","accessedAt":"2026-08-20T21:35:58.016Z","confidence":"official","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.hillmanfoundation.org/hillman-prizes/us/honorees"},{"id":"source-award-record-national-book-awards-nonfiction-wikipedia-national-book-award-for-nonfiction","label":"Wikipedia: National Book Award for Nonfiction","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Book_Award_for_Nonfiction","accessedAt":"2026-08-20T21:35:58.016Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official archive URL: https://www.nationalbook.org/national-book-awards/search/ Imported table: National Book Award for Nonfiction winners and finalists, 2020–2029"},{"id":"source-open-library-the-rise-and-fall-of-the-third-reich-william-l-shirer","label":"Open Library metadata for The Rise and Fall of the Third Reich","url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL23128028M","accessedAt":"2026-05-12T22:45:40.796Z","